cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Not All Bad Demonstrations Are Equally Bad: Quantifying How Demonstration Failure Modes Degrade Closed-Loop Policy Performance"
abstract: >-
  A controlled simulation study treating demonstration quality as the
  independent variable. Five failure modes are injected at controlled
  contamination rates into behaviour-cloning datasets for a 2D block-pushing
  task. Across two policy families, ten paired seeds, and transition-matched
  controls, the study compares open-loop error with closed-loop task success.
